kiln carries Bun to run its UI server. This folder holds what that brings with it, and travels
with it inside the kiln binary.

Bun 1.4.3, the official release for this platform (https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/releases/tag/bun-v1.4.3)
  Bun itself is MIT-licensed. It statically links JavaScriptCore and WebKit, which are LGPL-2
  licensed, and other libraries under their own licenses: see licenses/bun-LICENSE.md. The patched
  WebKit Bun links: https://github.com/oven-sh/webkit. Bun's source: https://github.com/oven-sh/bun
  (tag bun-v1.4.3).

On Linux, the musl runtime that Bun's musl build runs on, from Alpine Linux 3.24.2:

musl 1.2.6 (Alpine package musl-1.2.6-r2): lib/ld-musl-<arch>.so.1
  MIT license: see licenses/musl-COPYRIGHT. Source: https://musl.libc.org/releases/musl-1.2.6.tar.gz
  and Alpine's build of it: https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports/-/tree/3.24-stable/main/musl

libstdc++ and libgcc_s from GCC 15.2.0 (Alpine packages libstdc++-15.2.0-r5 and libgcc-15.2.0-r5):
lib/libstdc++.so.6 and lib/libgcc_s.so.1
  GNU General Public License version 3 or later, with the GCC Runtime Library Exception 3.1: see
  licenses/GPL-3.0 and licenses/GCC-RUNTIME-LIBRARY-EXCEPTION. Corresponding source:
  https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/gcc/gcc-15.2.0/gcc-15.2.0.tar.xz and Alpine's build of it:
  https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports/-/tree/3.24-stable/main/gcc
